  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-11-15T16:07:40.420Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "A handful of people have me blocked, and while I would much rather work things out with them, if they're going to have me blocked I'd rather not have them presented in front of me like that.\n\nThis bug first appeared in 1004, however it seems to be at least fixed on the side of the blocking party -- they can no longer hear me speak as they once did. However, even up until now (1010), the blocked party can still see them. Furthermore, there appears to be some issues with the social menu arising as well.\n\nTo give more detail on how the bug can be reproduced:\n\n- If the blocked party joins *after* the party that blocked them, they will be able to see and hear them.\n\n- If, however, the party that blocked them joins after the blocked party, then all appears to work as intended with the exception of sometimes being able to locate their player capsule with the pointer (a long-standing bug of VRChat from what I know, this has been a case for ages. See here: https://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/916-blocked-users-capsules-are-selectable\n\n- Lastly, in scenario 2, an issue with the social menu arises -- the blocked party cannot even see the person that blocked them in the social menu. I've had this happen a couple times where I was DMed about the presence of someone in the room that I didn't notice because I couldn't even check my social menu for them.\n\nIf the third is, by chance, an intended new behavior for how blocking is supposed to work, then I'd have to protest that a bit -- even between two people who have eachother blocked, they still want to be able to know if someone they've blocked is in the room, and it also makes unblocking someone a bigger pain to do from the client (especially if their name contains special characters and is thus unsearchable). Furthermore instance owners lose the ability to moderate their room if someone they've blocked joins. However, I assume this is not an intended behavior.\n\nI don't know if this is still a widespread issue or not, or if I'm one of just a few outliers experiencing this. Most complaints about blocking issues seems to have subsided by now, however perhaps the uproar has simply died down because things have been fixed for the people who do the blocking which is the side that would obviously be more upset by the situation. In any case it's a bug I felt needs pointed out, while I rather just not be blocked this is making what is already an awkward feeling situation even more awkward. (I actually blocked them all back for a bit because it made me uncomfortable, but I withdrew those blocks because I don't want them getting the wrong idea that I'm being toxic or something).\n\nI have screenshot proof of the situation if they're desired, but opting not to show them here as to not publicly disclose who I have personal drama with.\n\nI believe this report is related, however it's for an older build: https://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/blocked-users-can-still-see-you\n\nThanks!",
